 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Usually there's groom's side and a bride's side, and each covers half. Some couples also add friends and family fund to cover anything left. That's honest and easy. Just let them know you'd love their support but you' sort it on your own too. Not at all. It shows they' welcome to help, but you're happy with your plan. Then you can thank them sincerely and move on. Some couples say yes to split costs, and yes to having the bride and groom's families pay. That's the wise thing to do. Then it' your wedding day, not theirs. Tell them when you get married.",
